invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide_edwards.h
catches: x25519_equiv_test
reason: select_entry swaps y + x and y - x for a negative digit and keeps
  2dxy, so it adds (-x, y) with the T term of (x, y): a point that is on
  no curve. Every scalar with a negative digit, which is almost every
  scalar, gives a wrong key, and bin/x25519_equiv_test holds the key
  generation to both ladders.

--- old
        o->xy2d[w] ^= negative_mask & (o->xy2d[w] ^ minus);
--- new
        o->xy2d[w] ^= 0 & negative_mask & (o->xy2d[w] ^ minus);
